WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.4 · Financial Management
Restricted and unrestricted funds

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Know which money is committed to what, from the first grant or gift with conditions.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
Some money can be used only for a purpose a funder set; other money you can use for anything within your mission. The kind of money decides who can change how it is spent.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Four kinds of money

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:39.722
Restricted: Only for the purpose the funder or donor set; changes need their written agreement. For example: The US$6,000 youth-fund grant may only pay for trainee wages and mentoring.

6
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:49.200
Unrestricted: Your initiative decides how to use it, within its mission. For example: Stall and café sales, plus the founders’ own US$4,000 of savings.

7
00:00:49.200 --> 00:01:01.641
Designated: Unrestricted money the founders set aside for a purpose; they can change that decision themselves. For example: Our bakery sets money aside each month towards its own shop in year two.

8
00:01:01.641 --> 00:01:14.170
Deferred: Money received in advance, earned only when you deliver the work or goods. For example: The office canteen pays a month of bread upfront, delivered over four weeks.

9
00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.170
Why the kind matters

10
00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:21.956
1. Using restricted money elsewhere, even for weeks, can break the agreement or the law.

11
00:01:21.956 --> 00:01:27.259
2. Flexible money is what covers your core costs and risks.

12
00:01:27.259 --> 00:01:33.563
3. Funders trust initiatives that can show where their money went.

13
00:01:33.963 --> 00:01:34.563
What it feeds into

14
00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:40.237
1. Your funds register: one code per restricted fund, with its balance.

15
00:01:40.237 --> 00:01:45.541
2. Your bookkeeping and funder reports, recording spending against each code.

16
00:01:45.541 --> 00:01:51.844
3. Your cash flow and reserves, which rely on flexible money.

17
00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:52.844
What to avoid

18
00:01:52.844 --> 00:01:58.148
Reading the grant conditions after accepting the money, not before.

19
00:01:58.148 --> 00:02:03.081
Treating pre-orders or advance fees as money already earned.

20
00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:09.385
Relying almost entirely on restricted money, with little flexible income.

21
00:02:09.985 --> 00:02:11.785
You set up your funds register, even with one or two lines.

22
00:02:11.785 --> 00:02:15.785
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:17.285 --> 00:02:20.385
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
